00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:32.040
I'm not a licensed financial advisor, and this isn't financial advice.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:35.520
Always do your own research before putting real money to work.

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:42.280
Friday's S&amp;P 500 Clothes landed at 7,580, down 1.8%.

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:55.480
The NASDAQ composite closed at 25,437, down 2.9%, up 9.47% year-to-date, and up 13.69% since March 16, 2026.

00:00:55.480 --> 00:01:03.740
statistics. The Toronto Stock Exchange Composite closed at 35,620, down 1.7%. Technology

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:08.080
led the sell-off for a third straight week as artificial intelligence names gave back

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:14.020
earlier gains. The Bank of Canada next sets its overnight rate target on December 9, with

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:19.720
the market pricing and steady policy. 14 days ago, the simulated end bridge hold, ticker

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:26.360
ENB, printed an earnings beat from volume growth, yet it still closed down 0.21%.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:30.948
Valuation screening is how you hunt for a discount inside that kind of tape.

00:01:31.528 --> 00:01:36.248
You compare current forward price to earnings, and price to sales multiples against a five-year

00:01:36.248 --> 00:01:41.588
historical average, and against sector peers, and you only keep names that sit cheap on both.

00:01:42.228 --> 00:01:47.028
Applied material supplies wafer fabrication equipment used to make advanced semiconductors,

00:01:47.028 --> 00:01:51.988
and according to Fool.com, its forward price to earnings multiple sits below the median

00:01:51.988 --> 00:01:57.408
recorded over the past five years, even as hyperscale operators accelerate capital budgets.

00:01:58.028 --> 00:02:04.008
Open a brokerage screener, input the ticker AMAT, open the valuation metrics tab, and

00:02:04.008 --> 00:02:08.948
read the 5-year percentile ranking column. A reading below the 40th percentile plus

00:02:08.948 --> 00:02:14.368
positive year-over-year order growth is the flag that earns a second look, not an automatic buy.

00:02:14.368 --> 00:02:19.008
Think of it like a commercial oven marked down at the restaurant supply store, the same

00:02:19.008 --> 00:02:21.468
week three new kitchens break ground on your street.

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:24.988
The discount only matters if those kitchens actually get built.

00:02:25.668 --> 00:02:31.048
The same screen delivered gains in 2023 when equipment suppliers re-rated after cloud providers

00:02:31.048 --> 00:02:37.048
published similar multi-year capital expenditure forecasts, and it produced losses in early 2022

00:02:37.468 --> 00:02:44.348
when rising rates compressed multiples across the semiconductor supply chain, even though

00:02:44.348 --> 00:02:49.888
You can run those identical thresholds inside a tax-free savings account or TFSA, so any

00:02:49.888 --> 00:02:54.748
later re-rating is deferred on the tax side while the quantitative bar stays the same.

00:02:55.448 --> 00:03:00.508
The method still requires that the discount line up with a verifiable sector catalyst, not

00:03:00.508 --> 00:03:02.348
with isolated multiple contraction.

00:03:03.467 --> 00:03:08.307
Applied materials is today's simulated weekly hold, and it is the valuation screen in

00:03:08.307 --> 00:03:09.027
live form.

00:03:09.027 --> 00:03:16.527
This is a simulated trade for learning purposes, shares only $1,000 NASDAQ listed, technology

00:03:16.527 --> 00:03:21.047
sector, judged against the NASDAQ composite over the same five sessions.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:26.367
Because this episode lands on a weekend, the entry is Monday's open under the published

00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:32.127
rules, a market on open order, and the hold runs five sessions unless the stop hits first.

00:03:32.687 --> 00:03:39.007
The stop sits 8% below entry, which caps the simulated loss at $80 on the $1,000 position

00:03:39.007 --> 00:03:43.227
and the target range is plus 3% to plus 7%.

00:03:43.227 --> 00:03:49.126
A daily close below the 200-day moving average on the daily chart kills the valuation support

00:03:49.126 --> 00:03:49.546
thesis.

00:03:50.166 --> 00:03:54.426
That is the invalidation, named now, so nobody invents a different one later.

00:03:55.046 --> 00:04:00.346
Two factors line up, the forward multiple below its five-year median, and the sector catalyst

00:04:00.346 --> 00:04:02.206
from accelerating data center budgets.

00:04:02.826 --> 00:04:04.946
Volume confirmation is the missing piece.

00:04:04.946 --> 00:04:10.546
Price sits above the 50-day moving average, but volume is only running near the 20-day average,

00:04:10.986 --> 00:04:13.006
so confidence is medium, not high.

00:04:13.606 --> 00:04:18.186
Apple's last hold already showed what happens when valuation support stands alone without

00:04:18.186 --> 00:04:19.746
sector rotation behind it.

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:24.826
And this week's technology tape is still in a third week of selling, so that lesson is

00:04:24.826 --> 00:04:26.306
doing real work on this grade.

00:04:26.826 --> 00:04:31.706
You see a name sitting below its 5-year-forward multiple during a 3-week sector sell-off,

00:04:31.986 --> 00:04:33.466
with volume stuck at average.

00:04:33.466 --> 00:04:37.206
Do you take the discount Monday or do you wait for the third factor?

00:04:37.706 --> 00:04:42.146
I am taking the simulated entry because the screen plus the catalyst are the two factors

00:04:42.146 --> 00:04:46.766
the rule book asked for this week, and I am keeping the grade at medium because volume

00:04:46.766 --> 00:04:47.706
never confirmed.

00:04:48.603 --> 00:04:54.803
A tracking error, not a market outcome, voided the FTG practice pick so no simulated result

00:04:54.803 --> 00:04:58.243
is claimed for it, and it is excluded from the running totals.

00:04:58.243 --> 00:05:04.203
Apple, ticker AAPL, was the earlier weekly hold we simulated buying at the Friday open

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:13.323
at $349.12, and it exited at the Thursday close at $348.91 after the full five sessions.

00:05:13.743 --> 00:05:19.803
The position laws 0.06%, 60 cents on the $1,000 simulated stake.

00:05:20.363 --> 00:05:27.543
The NASDAQ gained 1.12% over those same sessions, so alpha was minus 1.18%.

00:05:27.543 --> 00:05:34.223
Stated confidence was medium, the 200-day invalidation never mattered, and the 8% stop was not reached.

00:05:34.763 --> 00:05:42.703
The valuation thesis stayed intact the whole way, yet the name still lagged because broader technology rotation outweighed the single name catalyst,

00:05:43.303 --> 00:05:48.043
and medium was the right grade for a mixed setup that never had sector rotation confirmation.

00:05:48.723 --> 00:05:52.363
This one did not work in alpha terms, and the adjustment is simple.

00:05:52.363 --> 00:05:58.503
even when a multiple looks attractive, check whether the sector is actually attracting flows before the next open.

00:05:59.516 --> 00:06:04.416
Yahoo Finance is the fastest way to run the percentile screen we used on applied materials.

00:06:04.896 --> 00:06:09.616
You filter United States and Canadian equities by forward price to earnings percentile,

00:06:10.016 --> 00:06:12.916
versus five-year history, and versus the sector median.

00:06:13.496 --> 00:06:16.976
Set the percentile threshold below 40 and the sector to technology,

00:06:17.716 --> 00:06:21.256
and the five-year ranking prints in the results table in under two minutes.

00:06:21.256 --> 00:06:26.596
formats. Core valuation metrics sit on the free screener tab, no paid tier is required,

00:06:27.036 --> 00:06:31.836
which is why a TFSA investor can surface names like applied materials before the open

00:06:31.836 --> 00:06:38.774
without extra software. Interactive Broker's Trader Workstation, or TWS, adds the risk overlay

00:06:38.774 --> 00:06:44.234
the Yahoo table does not. The Globe and Mail notes that the TWS scanner can flag stocks

00:06:44.234 --> 00:06:49.514
where price sits below the 200-day moving average, yet free cash flow yield exceeds the

00:06:49.514 --> 00:06:54.754
sector average, with a secondary filter for positive year-over-year revenue growth, then

00:06:54.754 --> 00:06:56.674
export the list for position sizing.

00:06:57.254 --> 00:07:01.834
Set the scan to run at market open and root results to a watch list inside a registered

00:07:01.834 --> 00:07:02.274
account.

00:07:02.794 --> 00:07:05.294
That feature is on the free TWS platform.

00:07:05.834 --> 00:07:09.774
I have no financial relationship with Yahoo Finance or Interactive Brokers.

