Mark Carney is accelerating talks with non-United States partners, while United States trade negotiations

00:07:16.513 --> 00:07:23.173
continue. BNN Bloomberg reports, which cuts single-market risk for exporters and opens new revenue

00:07:23.173 --> 00:07:28.893
streams for Canadian firms with global supply chains. Industrials and materials exporters are the

00:07:28.893 --> 00:07:34.293
group most exposed to new bilateral deals that lower tariff barriers on intermediate goods,

00:07:34.673 --> 00:07:40.153
so review those TSX holdings and consider a broad international equity exchange traded fund,

00:07:40.153 --> 00:07:46.846
and such as SCHF inside a TFSA, United States corporate profits have reached the highest

00:07:46.846 --> 00:07:52.666
share of gross domestic products since 1929, the Globe and Mail reports, driven largely

00:07:52.666 --> 00:07:57.966
by technology spending. Elevated margins can compress if artificial intelligence costs

00:07:57.966 --> 00:08:03.066
rise faster than revenue, and the technology names with the largest recent margin expansion

00:08:03.066 --> 00:08:08.206
now trade at the widest premium to the broader market, which is why a trim and rotate toward

00:08:08.206 --> 00:08:12.066
more stable free cash flow profiles is the action on the table.

00:08:12.985 --> 00:08:16.905
Three major space firms report earnings across two days in early November,

00:08:17.525 --> 00:08:21.565
full.com notes, and that clustered schedule is a short window to compare

00:08:21.565 --> 00:08:25.525
order books and margin trends. Download each latest investor

00:08:25.525 --> 00:08:29.605
presentation, write down the prior quarter backlog to revenue ratio,

00:08:30.065 --> 00:08:33.885
add the three tickers to a watch list and compare revenue guidance versus

00:08:33.885 --> 00:08:40.327
consensus before the first release. Open AI secured only $11 billion of a planned $30

00:08:40.327 --> 00:08:46.267
billion round, investing.com reports, a sign of cooler appetite for late-stage artificial

00:08:46.267 --> 00:08:51.047
intelligence bets. Smaller funding can slow expansion plans and hit suppliers,

00:08:51.547 --> 00:08:56.587
so semi-conductor equipment manufacturers that had modeled continued hyperscale capital expenditure

00:08:56.587 --> 00:09:02.847
growth may see downward revisions to forward orders if the shortfall persists. Watch those order

00:09:02.847 --> 00:09:08.745
prints over the next two quarters. The rules-based record shows a matched window alpha versus the

00:09:08.745 --> 00:09:16.465
NASDAQ of minus 0.41% across 42 trades. 20 of those 42 trades beat the index over their own

00:09:16.465 --> 00:09:24.425
windows. The average trade return minus 0.58% against the NASDAQ's minus 0.17% over the same

00:09:24.425 --> 00:09:31.505
sessions. And a T statistic of minus 0.43 means the result is not yet distinguishable from luck.

00:09:31.505 --> 00:09:38.545
The full history since March 2026 covers 93 trades with a 52% wind rate and cumulative

00:09:38.545 --> 00:09:46.165
profit of $52.20, and the current cold streak sits $378.93 below its peak.

00:09:46.885 --> 00:09:52.605
Each $1,000 trade runs independently under fixed five session holds, next open entries

00:09:52.605 --> 00:09:58.285
and stop or horizon exits, so the matched window number is the only apples to apples comparison,

00:09:58.285 --> 00:10:04.345
and the analysis is tightening confirmation after this stretch rather than treating the sample as a finished edge.

00:10:05.099 --> 00:10:11.819
You hold Celestica ahead of its next quarterly release and you rest a limit order to add on any dip below the recent low.

00:10:12.319 --> 00:10:19.619
The report shows revenue up 12% yet free cash flow down 8% because capital spending on new facilities rose sharply.

00:10:20.259 --> 00:10:24.219
A cruel accounting lets a company recognize revenue before the cash arrives.

00:10:24.219 --> 00:10:28.719
While heavy capital expenditure drains the balance sheet even when the income statement

00:10:28.719 --> 00:10:29.439
looks healthy.

00:10:29.979 --> 00:10:31.679
Revenue is the invoice you sent.

00:10:32.179 --> 00:10:35.959
Free cash flow is the deposit that actually hit after you paid for the new kitchen.

00:10:36.619 --> 00:10:41.679
Open the cash flow statement first, subtract capital expenditures from operating cash flow,

00:10:42.039 --> 00:10:45.399
and compare that free cash flow number to the same quarter last year.

00:10:45.939 --> 00:10:50.539
A drop of more than 10% despite revenue growth is the signal that the company is spending

00:10:50.539 --> 00:10:51.419
ahead of returns.

00:10:51.419 --> 00:10:56.259
concerns. The common misconception is that a revenue or earnings per share beat automatically

00:10:56.259 --> 00:11:01.839
means the stock will rise. The fixes to require both an earnings beat and year-over-year free

00:11:01.839 --> 00:11:07.179
cash flow growth before adding to the position. Celestica's place in artificial intelligence

00:11:07.179 --> 00:11:12.839
data center supply chains makes that check especially sharp, because recent expansion announcements

00:11:12.839 --> 00:11:17.639
have come with elevated capital expenditures that have not yet shown up as proportional

00:11:17.639 --> 00:11:22.519
free cash flow gains. Skip the reconciliation and you often find later that

00:11:22.519 --> 00:11:26.819
reported earnings growth was funded by balance sheet expansion rather than

00:11:26.819 --> 00:11:30.999
operating leverage and the multiple compresses once the market prices the

00:11:30.999 --> 00:11:35.519
higher reinvestment need. The same discipline applies to any TSX listed

00:11:35.519 --> 00:11:40.299
technology name whose growth story rests on multi-year infrastructure contracts.

00:11:40.919 --> 00:11:44.799
Remember an earnings beat funded by the balance sheet is not the same as an

00:11:44.799 --> 00:11:50.261
earnings beat funded by the business. Open your brokerage screener, set forward price

00:11:50.261 --> 00:11:54.961
to earnings below the five-year median and sector to technology, add the top three

00:11:54.961 --> 00:12:00.381
names to a watch list inside your TFSA, and then spend under 10 minutes on each cashflow

00:12:00.381 --> 00:12:05.821
statement, comparing the latest quarter to the year ago period. Before we wrap, Monday's

00:12:05.821 --> 00:12:10.861
open is the simulated applied materials entry, and I will be watching whether volume in the

00:12:10.861 --> 00:12:14.681
equipment names finally steps above that 20-day average on the first session.

